  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published study pair MD simulations with HDX-MS and AI-assisted modeling to interpret structural and dynamic data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of molecular dynamics and related computational modeling to interpret experimental structural and dynamic observables. PHENOMS couples backbone hydrogen-bond network analysis of MD trajectories with HDX-MS. A separate preprint introduces multi-ensemble maximum-entropy reweighting to handle shared peptide-dependent deuterium loss in differential HDX-MS, validated on LeuT and NCX_Mj. A third preprint applies an AI protein co-scientist with Boltz-2, rDock, AlphaFold3 and HDOCK to OGT TPR deletions and XLID-associated substitutions. The published study combines MD simulations with neural relational inference to identify a conserved βα5-βα7 dynamic coupling sector in thermophilic GH1 β-glucosidases. What is new is the coupling of ensemble-based reweighting and hydrogen-bond analysis to HDX-MS readouts, and the extension of AI-assisted modeling to disease-variant mutants.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
